# Facade methods that deliberately have no COM counterpart.
#
# Read by check_api_drift.ps1, which fails on any public method of a mapped interface in
# MsgFacade.h that reaches no method in MsgcoreCom.idl. Format, one per line:
#
#     <pair id>  <Interface>::<Method>     # why the server does not carry it
#
# THE BAR HERE IS HIGHER THAN A REASON. MsgFacade.h states a 1:1 intent in its own design
# rules -- every method maps onto a [dual] interface method, LPCWSTR->BSTR,
# void*+size->SAFEARRAY(VT_UI1). So an entry in this file is not merely an exemption; it
# is an exception to a written promise, and it should either say why the promise does not
# reach this method, or be the prompt to reword the promise. "Not needed by scripting
# clients" is a reason. "Not done yet" is a to-do wearing a reason's clothes -- write it
# as UNTRIAGED so it is counted with the others.
#
# Automation cannot express everything a vtable can, and that is the honest bulk of what
# belongs here: a method taking a void* the marshaller has no VARIANT for, an out-param
# whose lifetime a script cannot hold, a callback registered rather than sourced. Say
# which, so the next reader can tell a marshalling limit from a decision.
#
# UNTRIAGED marks a line banked by -Seed on the day the check was first run. It means
# only that nobody has looked yet, and it is counted out loud on every run.
#
# What this file cannot cover: interfaces the COM server carries that the facade has no
# type for. IMsgAttrCom and IMsgDescCom are a node's ATTR and CHILD scopes -- scopes in
# the facade, interfaces in COM -- and this check runs upstream to downstream only, so
# neither will ever appear here. That gap is stated in the config beside this file.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  UNTRIAGED -- banked by -Seed, not decided by anybody.
#
#  Each line below says only that the member had no counterpart on the day the
#  check was first run. Replacing UNTRIAGED with a real reason IS the triage, and
#  the count is printed on every run so the backlog cannot go quiet.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
facade-to-com  IMsgCursor::GetKind    # UNTRIAGED (method, include/MsgFacade.h:536)
facade-to-com  IMsgCursor::GetNode    # UNTRIAGED (method, include/MsgFacade.h:542)
facade-to-com  IMsgCursor::IsEnd    # UNTRIAGED (method, include/MsgFacade.h:532)
